Design brief — go for genuinely award-winning, editorial, high-craft, not a generic bootstrap gradient:
- Deep, rich, dark-first canvas (near-black with a subtle colour cast), with three large soft-blurred colour orbs (violet, cyan, warm magenta/amber) slowly drifting and scaling on independent long-duration keyframes behind the card — a real aurora, heavy blur radii, mix-blend-mode where it helps.
- .grain: a CSS-only fine noise/texture overlay (e.g. repeating-conic or repeating-linear micro-pattern at very low opacity, or a tiny inline SVG data URI feTurbulence in a background-image) plus an optional subtle vignette, to kill the flat plastic look.
- .card: premium glassmorphism — backdrop-filter blur+saturate behind @supports with a solid fallback, 1px translucent gradient border (border-image or a ::before mask trick), layered shadows (large ambient + tight contact), generous asymmetric padding, ~24-32px radius, and a soft specular highlight sweeping the top edge.
- .eyebrow: tiny uppercase, heavy letter-spacing, muted, with a small glowing dot or rule; .title: restrained mid-size, tight tracking, medium contrast — it must NOT compete with the message.
- .message: the hero moment. Huge fluid clamp() display type (roughly clamp(2.75rem, 11vw, 7rem)), tight line-height and negative letter-spacing, animated gradient text (background-clip:text) with a slow shimmer pass, plus a soft coloured text glow.
- States: [data-state="loading"] shows a shimmering skeleton bar in place of .message and a pulsing .status; [data-state="ready"] triggers a staggered entrance — eyebrow, title, message, status, meta rising and fading in sequence with a spring-ish cubic-bezier, and the meta__dot pulsing green; [data-state="error"] shifts the palette to red/amber, tints the card border and glow, and makes .status a legible monospace error pill with a red dot.
- Fluid responsive at every width (360px phone to ultrawide), :focus-visible ring, light palette via prefers-color-scheme: light that is equally considered (warm off-white, soft pastel orbs, ink text) — not an afterthought, and prefers-reduced-motion: reduce disabling all animation while keeping the static composition beautiful.

Taste bar: it should look like a modern product landing page from Linear/Vercel/Stripe, not a CodePen demo. Avoid rainbow gaudiness; pick a tight, confident palette and commit.

